data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan and implement the settings dashboard.

## Component Plan: Settings Dashboard

### Component Tree
```
Settings                   (page — owns activeSection, orchestrates layout)
├── SettingsSidebar        (vertical nav tabs, emits section changes)
├── ProfileSection         (profile editing with avatar preview)
├── NotificationsSection   (toggles and channel muting)
├── SecuritySection        (password change, 2FA, sessions)
│   └── (confirmation dialog inline)
└── AppearanceSection      (theme, font, language, compact, live preview)


```

The Settings page will manage the active section state, with each child component handling its own data fetching and updates through the ISettingsService. The sidebar will trigger section changes via callbacks, and I'll build the leaf components first before assembling them into the main page.

I'll organize the files under `/Components/Pages/Settings/` with Bootstrap styling for consistency with the app's design system.

```

csharp
// Models and service interface
namespace sv_1ca7ac621ae14efea1f83d5ac2d1d862.Models
{
    public class UserSettings
    {
        public string Theme { get; set; } = "light";
        public bool EmailNotifications { get; set; } = true;
        public bool PushNotifications { get; set; } = false;
        public string Language { get; set; } = "en";
        public bool TwoFactorEnabled { get; set; } = false;
    }
}

namespace sv_1ca7ac621ae14efea1f83d5ac2d1d862.Services
{
    public interface ISettingsService
    {
        Task<UserSettings> GetSettingsAsync();
        Task SaveSettingsAsync(UserSettings settings);
    }

    public class SettingsService : ISettingsService
    {
        public async Task<UserSettings> GetSettingsAsync()
        {
            // Simulate loading from storage
            return await Task.FromResult(new UserSettings());
        }

        public async Task SaveSettingsAsync(UserSettings settings)
        {
            // Simulate saving to storage
            await Task.CompletedTask;
        }
    }
}
```

Now I'll create the Razor components for the settings page and sections.
```razor
@* Settings.razor - Main settings page *@
@page "/settings"
@using sv_1ca7ac621ae14efea1f83d5ac2d1d862.Models
@using sv_1ca7ac621ae14efea1f83d5ac2d1d862.Services
@inject ISettingsService SettingsService

<div class="container-fluid mt-4">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-3">
            <SettingsSidebar @ref="sidebar" OnSectionChange="HandleSectionChange" />
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-9">
            @if (currentSettings != null)
            {
                @switch (activeSection)
                {
                    case "profile":
                        <ProfileSection Settings="currentSettings" OnSave="SaveSettings" />
                        break;
                    case "notifications":
                        <NotificationsSection Settings="currentSettings" OnSave="SaveSettings" />
                        break;
                    case "security":
                        <SecuritySection Settings="currentSettings" OnSave="SaveSettings" />
                        break;
                    case "appearance":
                        <AppearanceSection Settings="currentSettings" OnSave="SaveSettings" />
                        break;
                }
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private UserSettings currentSettings;
    private string activeSection = "profile";
    private SettingsSidebar sidebar;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        currentSettings = await SettingsService.GetSettingsAsync();
    }

    private void HandleSectionChange(string section)
    {
        activeSection = section;
    }

    private async Task SaveSettings()
    {
        await SettingsService.SaveSettingsAsync(currentSettings);
    }
}
```

```razor
@* SettingsSidebar.razor *@
<div class="list-group">
    <button class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" @onclick="() => OnSectionChange.InvokeAsync(\"profile\")">
        Profile
    </button>
    <button class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" @onclick="() => OnSectionChange.InvokeAsync(\"notifications\")">
        Notifications
    </button>
    <button class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" @onclick="() => OnSectionChange.InvokeAsync(\"security\")">
        Security
    </button>
    <button class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" @onclick="() => OnSectionChange.InvokeAsync(\"appearance\")">
        Appearance
    </button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSectionChange { get; set; }
}
```

